a-win-for-beach-access/articleshow/134136966.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-12T19:48:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134137264,imgsize-127913.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[She began college in 1930; 77 years later, Nola Ochs became the world's oldest graduate]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134125955.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Nola Ochs, celebrating her 95th birthday, made headlines as the oldest college graduate in the world after earning her bachelor's degree from Fort Hays State University. Her academic pursuits began in 1930, but she put her education on hold to raise a family. At 98, she didn't stop there and accomplished the incredible feat of earning her master's degree, symbolizing a powerful testament to lifelong commitment to education.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1930-she-took-her-first-college-course-during-the-great-depression-in-2007-she-finally-received-her-bachelors-degree-what-made-nola-ochs-worlds-oldest-graduate/articleshow/134125955.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1930-she-took-her-first-college-course-during-the-great-depression-in-2007-she-finally-received-her-bachelors-degree-what-made-nola-ochs-worlds-oldest-graduate/articleshow/134125955.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-12T19:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134126906,imgsize-683509.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Donald Trump's childhood home was bought for $835,000 in 2025; it has sold for $1.93 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134128572.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The childhood home of Donald Trump, located in Queens, has been sold for an impressive $1.93 million. Originally bought for $835,000, this Tudor-style property underwent extensive renovations over eight months, transforming it into a contemporary five-bedroom residence. With ties to Trump's early years, its historical significance has notably heightened its market value.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/donald-trumps-childhood-home-was-bought-for-835000-in-2025-after-a-500000-renovation-it-has-sold-for-1-93-million/articleshow/134128572.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/donald-trumps-childhood-home-was-bought-for-835000-in-2025-after-a-500000-renovation-it-has-sold-for-1-93-million/articleshow/134128572.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-12T19:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-134129465,imgsize-1751464.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Steve Jobs’ 17,250-sq-ft mansion was demolished after a long legal battle]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/134126048.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-1984-steve-jobs-bought-a-30-room-17250-sq-ft-california-mansion-after-years-of-legal-battles-it-was-demolished-in-2011-while-its-pipe-organ-and-historic-fixtures-were-salvaged/articleshow/134126048.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-1984-steve-jobs-bought-a-30-room-17250-sq-ft-california-mansion-after-years-of-legal-battles-it-was-demolished-in-2011-while-its-pipe-organ-and-historic-fixtures-were-salvaged/articleshow/134126048.cm